{"ts":"2026-10-04T17:31:55.731Z","run":"r2","cycle":22,"src":"orchestrator","type":"lesson","text":"A 20+ minute verification (stress suite) must start at the very top of a cycle, alone; when the runner ends a cycle it kills background runs, so two cycles in a row lost their stress results and orphaned test processes","topic":"cycles"}
{"ts":"2026-10-04T17:31:56.119Z","run":"r2","cycle":22,"src":"orchestrator","type":"lesson","text":"Run the long resilience suite in the main checkout and send fix workers to git worktrees told to run only targeted tests; parallel full test runs on a /mnt (WSL) drive caused load-induced flakes that were misread as product bugs","topic":"checks"}
{"ts":"2026-10-04T17:31:56.500Z","run":"r2","cycle":22,"src":"orchestrator","type":"lesson","text":"The cheap mechanical checker role (small model, 20-turn cap) cannot babysit long scripts or more than ~3 commands; the orchestrator should run long checks itself in the background and give qa short, redirected commands (cmd > file 2>&1; echo exit=$?)","topic":"roles"}
